; TicMambo configuration.
;
; Format: Keyword Value. Keywords are case insensitive.
; Lines starting with ';' or '#' are comments.
; Periods are whole days. Yes/No are boolean values.
; The file is read as UTF-8 or, if it is not valid UTF-8, in the system
; encoding (the ANSI code page on Windows).

; Directory where the mailer puts received tics and files. TicMambo looks
; here for the file named in each tic and for its copies that the mailer
; renamed (file.zip.1, file.zi0 and so on); a matching copy is moved to
; DestPath under the name from the tic. Required.
;
InboundPath d:\fido\inbound

; Directory where good files are moved together with their tics. Set it as
; the inbound in your file echo processor's config. Required. Must be
; different from InboundPath.
;
DestPath d:\fido\inbound\fecho

; Encoding of file names in tics. Names are converted from it to the file
; system encoding. A tic that is not valid in this encoding is logged and
; left alone. Default: cp866.
;
;TicCharset cp866

; Whether to ignore case when comparing file names from a tic with the
; files in InboundPath. With No, FILE.ZIP in a tic does not match file.zip,
; even on Windows. Keywords in tics are always case insensitive.
; Default: Yes on Windows, No elsewhere.
;
;IgnoreCase Yes

; Which time stamp of a tic gives its age (see WaitForFileDays and
; WaitForHiddenTicDays). Yes - its creation time. No - its modification
; time on Windows and its inode change time (ctime) elsewhere. Creation
; time is supported on Windows and on Linux (via statx(2), if syscall.ph is
; available and the file system stores creation time); where it is not,
; ctime is used. Default: Yes.
;
;UseCreationTime Yes

; How many days a tic waits for a file that matches its Crc and Size.
; After that the tic is moved to DestPath without a file or deleted (see
; DeleteOrphanTics). Default: 3.
;
;WaitForFileDays 3

; What to do with a tic whose file has not arrived within WaitForFileDays.
; Yes - delete it. No - move it to DestPath without a file. Files that
; don't match any tic are never touched. Default: No.
;
;DeleteOrphanTics No

; Windows: how many days to skip a tic that has the hidden attribute,
; since it may still be being received. After that it is processed as
; usual. 0 - do not skip. Files and tics moved to DestPath always have the
; attribute cleared. Default: 7.
;
;WaitForHiddenTicDays 7

; Whether to set the modification time of a good file to the current time
; when it is moved to DestPath. Default: No.
;
;TouchFiles No

; Windows: whether to put the short (8.3) name of the file into File, for
; file echo processors that only understand File and open the file by its
; short name. This is done when the file was found by Lfile or Fullname
; that differs from File and the short name that Windows gave the file in
; DestPath differs from File (ignoring case). If the file has no short
; name (8.3 names are disabled on the volume), the tic is left as it is and
; a warning is logged. Ignored on other systems. Default: No.
;
;FixShortName No

; Whether to add Fullname with the value of Lfile to tics that have Lfile
; but no Fullname, for file echo processors that understand Fullname but
; not Lfile. Default: No.
;
;AddFullname No

; What to do when a file or tic with the same name is already in DestPath
; or CorruptTicPath. No - leave the tic and its file in InboundPath until
; the next run; if this happens in DestPath, the exit code is 2. Yes -
; overwrite. This is not safe: a file moved earlier in the same run may be
; overwritten too, leaving its tic with another file. Default: No.
;
;OverwriteExisting No

; Maximum size of a tic in bytes. Larger tics are considered corrupt.
; Default: 65536.
;
;MaxTicSize 65536

; What to do with corrupt tics. A tic is corrupt if it is larger than
; MaxTicSize, contains NUL characters, has no File, Lfile or Fullname, has
; no Crc, has a Size that is not a decimal number or a Crc that is not a
; hexadecimal number of up to 8 digits, or names a file with a path, a
; drive letter, control characters, '.', '..', a device name such as CON
; or NUL, or a name ending in .tic.
;   Move   - move to CorruptTicPath;
;   Delete - delete;
;   Keep   - leave in place (log only).
; Default: Move.
;
;CorruptTicAction Move

; Directory where corrupt tics are moved. Required with CorruptTicAction
; Move. Must be different from InboundPath.
;
CorruptTicPath d:\fido\inbound\corrupt

; Log file, written in UTF-8. If not set, the log goes to stderr.
;
LogFile d:\fido\log\ticmambo.log

; How much to log: error, warning, info or debug. Default: info.
;
;LogLevel info
